<title>HUNGARY: GM TO SUPPLY POLISH CAR PLANT FROM HUNGARY.</title>
<headline>GM TO SUPPLY POLISH CAR PLANT FROM HUNGARY.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said on Monday it planned to supply painted car bodies from its Hungarian plant to its car assembly plant in the Polish capital Warsaw, starting with a couple of hundred units this year.</p>
<p>Deliveries, which could reach 15,000-20,000 units in 1998, likely will continue until GM's bigger plant in southern Poland is fully operational, GM said at a news conference.</p>
<p>The bigger plant in Poland is scheduled to open by 1999.</p>
<p>-- Ryan Tutak, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
